{
  "id": "product.sticky-tabs",
  "kind": "section",
  "name": "Sticky anchor tabs over autotab panels",
  "purpose": "Lets visitors jump between the main solution/feature areas of a long page via a sticky anchor bar, each area presenting its sub-capabilities in a tabbed slider.",
  "category": "product",
  "designSystem": "marketing",
  "implementedBy": "src/components/sections/StickyTabs.jsx",
  "description": "One component with a `variant` prop: 'solutions' (/lms/solutions) and 'features' (/lms/features). A sticky (top 0, z 999) bar of equal anchor pills (green when its panel is in view, scroll-spy) sits over a stack of panels; each panel is a header plus a tab row ABOVE a loop slider whose slides hold one paragraph, a fixed primary button ('Learn more' on solutions, 'Explore' on features) and a clipped product shot. 'solutions' headers are eyebrow + H4-style heading + paragraph beside a bordered stat card (40%); its bar sits in a 45.25rem container and its 5th anchor targets the sector-tabs block further down. 'features' headers are eyebrow / title / paragraph, bar in container-medium. <=767 the anchor bar and tab rows scroll horizontally (200px pills, 150px at <=479) and the stat card stacks under the copy.",
